{
  "source": "Chromium 141.0.7390.37, Linux, Playwright 中打开 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pythagorean_theorem，选中 p:has(math) 到 p:has(math) 后 Ctrl+C",
  "types": {
    "text/plain": "The theorem can be written as an equation relating the lengths of the sides a, b and the hypotenuse c, sometimes called the Pythagorean equation:[2]\na\n2\n+\nb\n2\n=\nc\n2\n.\n{\\displaystyle a^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2}.}The theorem is named for the Greek philosopher Pythagoras, born around 570 BC. The theorem has been proved numerous times by many different methods – possibly the most for any mathematical theorem. The proofs are diverse, including both geometric proofs and algebraic proofs, with some dating back thousands of years.",
